Article 11 Government departments shall designate the government data sharing working body of their own departments. The government data sharing working body shall be responsible for the specific work of government data sharing within its department and shall perform the following duties:
(1) organizing the compilation, updating, and maintenance of the government data catalog of its department;
(2) organizing the submission of government data sharing applications from its department, organizing the review of sharing applications involving its department's data, and coordinating and sharing its department's government data;
(3) ensuring that the government data provided by its department complies with government data sharing standards and specifications;
(4) organizing the submission or processing of data verification applications involving its department;
(5) establishing and improving the data security and personal information protection system in its department's government data sharing, and organizing the security assessment of its department's government data sharing;
(6) other work of its department related to government data sharing.

Article 14 Government data is divided into three categories based on sharing attributes: unconditional sharing, conditional sharing, and no sharing:
(1) government data that can be provided to all government departments for sharing and use belongs to the unconditional sharing category;
(2) government data that can be provided to relevant government departments for sharing and use under certain conditions belongs to the conditional sharing category;
(3) government data that, as expressly provided by laws, administrative regulations, and decisions of the State Council, cannot be provided to other government departments for sharing and use belongs to the no-sharing category.

Article 39 Where a government data provider department violates the provisions of these Regulations and falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of government data sharing at the same level shall order it to make corrections; if it refuses to correct or the circumstances are serious, the responsible leaders and directly responsible personnel shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) failing to compile or update the government data catalog as required;
(2) obstructing or affecting government data sharing by arbitrarily adding conditions or through other means;
(3) failing to cooperate with the data source department in promptly improving and updating government data;
(4) failing to respond to a government data sharing application on time or failing to share government data on time without proper justification;
(5) failing to return the government data within the administrative region of a lower-level government collected and generated by the business information system to the lower-level government department as required;
(6) failing to verify and correct in a timely manner after receiving a government data verification request;
(7) arbitrarily terminating or altering the government data sharing services already provided;
(8) failing to incorporate the already built government data platform into the national integrated government big data system as required;
(9) other circumstances violating the provisions of these Regulations.

Article 40 Where a government data demand department violates the provisions of these Regulations and falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of government data sharing at the same level shall order it to make corrections; if it refuses to correct or the circumstances are serious, the responsible leaders and directly responsible personnel shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) repeatedly collecting government data that can be obtained through sharing;
(2) arbitrarily exceeding the scope of use or using government data obtained through sharing for purposes beyond the sharing purpose;
(3) arbitrarily providing government data obtained through sharing to a third party;
(4) failing to properly dispose of government data obtained through sharing as required after the sharing purpose has been achieved, cannot be achieved, or is no longer necessary for achieving the sharing purpose;
(5) failing to preserve the records related to government data obtained through sharing as required;
(6) failing to fulfill the security management responsibility for government data obtained through sharing;
(7) other circumstances violating the provisions of these Regulations.

Article 41 Where the competent department of government data sharing violates the provisions of these Regulations and falls under any of the following circumstances, the people's government at the same level or the competent department at the higher level shall order it to make corrections; if it refuses to correct or the circumstances are serious, the responsible leaders and directly responsible personnel shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) failing to designate a data source department as required;
(2) failing to coordinate and handle government data sharing disputes as required;
(3) other circumstances violating the provisions of these Regulations.
